  "answer": "### Short Answer\nAn individual with ₱250,000 gross compensation income in 2024 is not required to file an income tax return, as their income falls within the tax-exempt threshold.\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThis is governed by Section 24 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), which states that individuals with a taxable income not exceeding ₱250,000 are exempt from income tax.\n\n### Interpretation\nUnder Section 24(A)(1) of the NIRC, the income tax rates for individuals specify that for the taxable year 2023 and onwards, individuals earning not over ₱250,000 are subject to a 0% tax rate. Therefore, if an individual's gross compensation income is exactly ₱250,000, they do not incur any tax liability.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nAs a result, individuals earning ₱250,000 or less from compensation are not required to file an income tax return, provided they have no other sources of income that would necessitate filing. This simplifies compliance for low-income earners, allowing them to avoid the administrative burden of filing a return when their income is below the taxable threshold.",
